---
description: API layering and the required sequence for endpoint changes.
globs: apps/api/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow `.claude/skills/add-endpoint/SKILL.md` for any route change.

- Use cases never import express or drizzle. They take plain input and return
  plain output. `import-x/no-restricted-paths` enforces this; if your import is
  rejected, the fix is a port in `ports.ts`, not an eslint-disable.
- `container.ts` is the only file that constructs a repository or a use case.
- Every endpoint validates its input with a schema from `packages/contracts`.
- Errors are typed domain errors mapped to RFC 9457 problem responses whose
  `detail` says what the user should do next.
- No patient identifier in any log line or error message.
